All right, a ~a week ago, I asked about how you can get the following 
messages:

	You cannot trample the little dog!
	Adjama shouts: "Who dared dig into my shop?"
	Wow! Modern art!
	As your mind turns inwards on itself, you forget everything else.
	wizard, escaped the dungeon (with the amulet)
		(this one should actually have been:
		 	wizard,escaped(with the Amulet)
						)

Now, correct answers follow... hit "n" if you want to keep guessing



You cannot trample the little dog!
	Somebody got this right. I had jumping boots and tried to jump into
	the square that contained my pet...

Adjama shouts:"Who dared dig into my shop?"
	Quite a lot of people got close, but nobody got the exact right 
	answer, I think. You get this message, if you shoot at the shop
	wall with a wand of digging from a distance (from the outside,
	of course). Don't try it in a normal game, though, as the shopkeeper
	will get angry.

Wow! Modern art!
	Again, there were some who got close... the correct answer is indeed
	that you read a scroll of magical mapping when you are hallucinating
	- BUT note that the scroll must be cursed.

As your mind turns inwards, you forget everything else.
	I was surprised how easy this one turned out to be, as it took me
	quite a lot of time before I thought of trying it...
	It really is the message you get, if you have named your character
	Maud and read a scroll of amnesia.

wizard,escaped(with the Amulet)
	This is - fortunately - something that should be impossible in normal
	game. As I said, it was in wizard mode. It involved one impossible 
	wish:
		What do you wish for? magic portal
		A magic portal.
	(You cannot wish for magic portals, fountains, altars or such in 
	normal playing mode - I *think* - but you can wish for them in 
	wizard mode...)
	The magic portals produced by wishing will not function as a 
	magic portal should. Normallly, you will only cause the dungeon
	to collapse, if you enter one. In the endgame, however, you will
	*escape* it instead (the same happens in Sanctum, too, possibly
	in all non-main dungeons). 	
	Even if you don't use the magic portal, the dungeon will collapse
	as soon as a monster steps on it.
	I still don't know how to wish for magic portals that would 
	actually *work* :-)

All right, what bizarre experiments have *YOU* made...? :->

